senses.gloss:
1. आप् cl. 5. P. आप्नो॑ति [AV. ix, 5, 22, &c.], (perf. आप, aor. आपत्, fut. आप्स्यति, inf. आप्तुम्), Ā. (perf. 3. pl. आपिरे॑, RV. ix, 108, 4, p. pf. आपान॑, RV. ii, 34, 7, but also pres. p. आ॑प्नान, RV. x, 114, 7) to reach, overtake, meet with, fall upon, RV.; AV.; ŚBr. &c.;
to obtain, gain, take possession of RV.; AV. &c., MBh.; Mn. &c.;
to undergo, suffer, Mn.;
to fall, come to any one;
to enter, pervade, occupy;
to equal:
Pass. आप्यते, to be reached or found or met with or obtained;
to arrive at one's aim or end, become filled, TS. &c.:
Caus. P. आपयति, to cause to reach or obtain or gain, ChUp. &c.;
to cause any one to suffer;
to hit, Kathās. :
Desid. P. and Ā. ईप्सति and ईप्सते [Pāṇ. vii, 4, 55] to strive to reach or obtain, AV.; ŚBr.; MBh. &c.:
Desid. of the Caus. आपिपयिषति, to strive to reach, ŚBr.;
